{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/537804-the-heart-of-the-sardonyx-system-is-revealed-a-new-legend-begins","id":537804,"title":"The heart of the Sardonyx system is revealed; a new Legend begins!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-02T23:28:19-07:00","id":537804,"title":"The heart of the Sardonyx system is revealed; a new Legend begins!","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/codename-sardonyx-teaser-the-first/\" target=\"_blank\">Here ya go!</a><br /> <br /> I'm impressed; and that's not easy to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T02:18:22-07:00","id":537928,"title":"","content":"I, too, am impressed.<br /> <br /> The heart of the resolution system seems to be the <b>Effects</b> you purchase after succeeding. We know type and severity of injury are linked to them, I wonder what examples of other things are linked.<br /> <br /> Interesting how Mundane and Daredevil have different Momentum caps, does the cap reduce as you scale up in power? How does that interact with spending Momentum to activate powers?<br /> <br /> Exciting times ahead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T04:59:51-07:00","id":538077,"title":"","content":"I never picked up Scion 1e, but I'm very interested in the second edition. The basics of this system seems very solid. I'm interested in the idea of having to actually roll a success to get the bonus successes, and the idea of a failed roll being not just a straight failure by default, nor a successful one devoid of any complications. I'm looking forward to further information.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 06-03-2015, 08:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T08:21:24-07:00","id":538386,"title":"","content":"Very movie-like, and I especially like it In the sense that in moves or TV shows a failure will often pave the way for the story continuing. You usually don't have, say, a detective searching for a specific thing, failing to find it, and not finding something else that at least allows the investigation to continue.<br /> <br /> Complications are a <i>great</i> idea too: &quot;OK, you managed to shoot the guy, but since you didn't have enough successes to deal with the complication, the case he was holding broke and now [the macguffin] is rolling around perilously&quot;, &quot;you managed to grab the iron bar, stopping your fall, but the force has yanked off one side of it from the wall, so it will be a bit harder to reach the ledge above&quot;, &quot;Yeah, that car throw will likely kill the cyclops...that is,unless you would rather use some successes to prevent those bystanders over there from getting hurt&quot;, and so on.<br /> <br /> The idea of Momentum interest me as well. I have become very fond of the idea of systems with tools to influence the ebb-and-flow of the scene, the pacing, and it is great for me to see that both Scion and Exalted will have that in some form (though from what I gather Exalted will have it more for the combat scenes, instead of in general like Sardonyx seems to be shaping up).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T10:57:21-07:00","id":538550,"title":"","content":"Color me curious. Also, I've been waiting for Scion 2E for while now. Good to see its back on track.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T11:00:26-07:00","id":538557,"title":"","content":"Cool, it's finally here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Can any of the developers answer me this question: attributes - which ones will we see for Scion? Will we see the same as in oWoD or the same as in nWoD? Or even something different? How about the skill-list(s) for Origin/Hero?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/153-ebon-wolf","name":"Ebon Wolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T11:34:40-07:00","id":538636,"title":"","content":"Not going to spoil details yet, but it's a list that hasn't been seen before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T13:10:46-07:00","id":538698,"title":"","content":"Looks like Persuasion, Culture, Might, Brawl, Cunning, Pilot, Awareness, Reason and Enigmas and we know it has a physical/mental/social split.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T13:15:26-07:00","id":538701,"title":"","content":"We know more than that: we know that within each of the physical/mental/social categories, it has a Power/Control/Resistance split. That tells me that while it won't be <i>the same</i> as nWoD's attribute set, it will be closer to that than to the oWoD/Exalted attribute set.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T13:19:06-07:00","id":538706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/537804-the-heart-of-the-sardonyx-system-is-revealed-a-new-legend-begins?p=538701#post538701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We know more than that: we know that within each of the physical/mental/social categories, it has a Power/Control/Resistance split. That tells me that while it won't be <i>the same</i> as nWoD's attribute set, it will be closer to that than to the oWoD/Exalted attribute set.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it'll be the nWoD attributes renamed?<br /> <br /> Looking forward to hearing more, but I'm not completely sold on 2e from this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T13:42:25-07:00","id":538755,"title":"","content":"My question is about how (or if) the Tiers for Scion and Trinity will line up. Trinity 1e gives us a daredevil/psion/nova set of tiers, where daredevils are essentially action heroes: luckier than most, and a bit more resiliant, but still within the bounds of mortal men; scions started slinging around superhuman powers; and novas operated on a level where it took teams of psions to confront a single aberrant. As a <i>very</i> rough comparison, Scion's Heroes operate somewhere between psions and novas; demigods seem to operate on roughly the same level as most novas; and only the high-end novas would stand a chance of keeping up with Scion's gods. In terms of Sardonyx, does <b>Scion: Origin</b> give us that game's rough equivalent to daredevils; are Heroes recast at a lower \u201cpower level\u201d; or does Scion \u201cskip a Tier\u201d compared to Trinity, going straight from \u201cordinary people\u201d to \u201clow-level superhuman\u201d? <br /> <br /> Or is the tier system more elaborate than that? The article mentioned that <b>Mage Chronicler's Guide</b> was raided liberally for ideas, with the action/adventure section singled out as something that was a key inspiration for Sardonyx; but I also recall that book recasting Mage as a superhero game, complete with a scaling system that had IIRC a six-step ladder from \u201cordinary guys\u201d to \u201cgods walking the Earth\u201d. Did Sardonyx take inspiration from that to give us, in effect, multiple Tiers for each of Origin, Hero, Demigod, and God? Say, ordinary mortals and pre-Visitation Scions as tiers 0 and 1, starting Heroes and advanced Heroes as Tiers 2 and 3, and so on?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T13:45:11-07:00","id":538759,"title":"","content":"HEY THAT'S PRETTY GOOD OBSERVATIONS THERE DATAWEAVER. HMM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T13:46:50-07:00","id":538760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/537804-the-heart-of-the-sardonyx-system-is-revealed-a-new-legend-begins?p=538759#post538759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HEY THAT'S PRETTY GOOD OBSERVATIONS THERE DATAWEAVER. HMM.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, those are indeed good observations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T13:53:35-07:00","id":538765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/537804-the-heart-of-the-sardonyx-system-is-revealed-a-new-legend-begins?p=538706#post538706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So it'll be the nWoD attributes renamed?<br /> <br /> Looking forward to hearing more, but I'm not completely sold on 2e from this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect that there will be more to it than renaming; it's very possible to come up with different interpretations of what \u201cmental power\u201d means, for instance. <br /> <br /> Besides, I never got why the nWoD attribute set is a turn-off. I rather <i>like</i> the ease that it brings to deciding which attribute is most appropriate for the task at hand. If it's merely a case of it not being the oWoD attribute set, well, Sardonyx wasn't going to be using that anyway: that set is married to the Storyteller System which is owned by that Icelandic company that bought out White Wolf; Sardonyx is OPP's house system, and <i>cannot</i> be a clone of the Storyteller/ing systems, even if its heritage from said systems is readily apparent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T13:58:20-07:00","id":538769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/537804-the-heart-of-the-sardonyx-system-is-revealed-a-new-legend-begins?p=538759#post538759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HEY THAT'S PRETTY GOOD OBSERVATIONS THERE DATAWEAVER. HMM.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that means what I think it does, I'm glad: MCG's tier system always struck me as a good power-tier system given the page-count restrictions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T17:02:21-07:00","id":538949,"title":"","content":"I am very much intrigued by what I've seen thus far.<br /> <br /> Great job, devs! It's early, yet, but this looks like it'll be the perfect system for Scion! I'm totally unfamiliar with the system for Trinity, so I can't say for certain, but it certainly sounds like it will fit them very well, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T18:01:12-07:00","id":538976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/537804-the-heart-of-the-sardonyx-system-is-revealed-a-new-legend-begins?p=538769#post538769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that means what I think it does, I'm glad: MCG's tier system always struck me as a good power-tier system given the page-count restrictions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only is all of this very interesting and i'm going to fetch my MCG as we speak but its also the most amusing interaction I've read all day. Thanks for the smile guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T19:01:21-07:00","id":539045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/537804-the-heart-of-the-sardonyx-system-is-revealed-a-new-legend-begins?p=538765#post538765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect that there will be more to it than renaming; it's very possible to come up with different interpretations of what \u201cmental power\u201d means, for instance.<br /> <br /> Besides, I never got why the nWoD attribute set is a turn-off. I rather <i>like</i> the ease that it brings to deciding which attribute is most appropriate for the task at hand. If it's merely a case of it not being the oWoD attribute set, well, Sardonyx wasn't going to be using that anyway: that set is married to the Storyteller System which is owned by that Icelandic company that bought out White Wolf; Sardonyx is OPP's house system, and <i>cannot</i> be a clone of the Storyteller/ing systems, even if its heritage from said systems is readily apparent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm hoping, but until I see the list I'm under the 'why not just use a derivative of nWoD 2e' opinion, as it solved about nine tenths of the problems I had with nWoD and can scale to between 'intrigue' and 'action' by the builds players bring.<br /> <br /> They aren't, It's just I can move 1e Scion into the nWoD system (1e or 2e) with maybe a couple of hours work, ending up with a set of attributes I can actually understand (although I'd prefer Intelligence being renamed Logic or Reason, seeing as that's essentially what differentiates it from wits in my games) because of their simple setup and recognisable names. I'm a bit sad about the loss of Appearance as a stat (it makes a lot of sense, I'd argue that if it wasn't for the power/finesse/resistance setup of nWoD social should be Presence/Appearance/Composure, and it's how I use manipulation anyway), but I can live with the current spread.<br /> <br /> Although looking at the document again, the terms used feel like better terms for the nWoD attributes, so I'm mainly waiting until I can get a good look at the add-ons before I decide. This'll include the skill list and full scaling mechanic, because I'm a bit suspicious of what I've seen of the current scaling, and need a better explanation to fully grok it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T20:42:18-07:00","id":539130,"title":"","content":"This has definitely caught my attention.<br /> <br /> I'm really liking the lowered threshold for what needs a roll, complex but not overtly difficult actions and narratively awesome and unique actions can just be hand-waved to succeed.<br /> <br /> The Momentum mechanic kinda reminds me of the destiny pool in the Fantasy Flight Star Wars RPG where there is some back and forth in that pool between the players and the Director. Should go a long way to help set a rhythm of uncertainty in scenes as both side are driven to try harder by their failures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T07:51:31-07:00","id":539524,"title":"","content":"Mundane is probably going to be the same for Origins. Daredevil will probably be the same for Hero. So the TN will be 8 for that. I think that they may use 7 for the TN for Demi-god and, lastly, 6 for the full fledged dieties. This makes it where Apollo would have an easier time of getting 6 successes with a pool of 10 dice than, say, Jeb the Janitor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T11:00:37-07:00","id":539735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/537804-the-heart-of-the-sardonyx-system-is-revealed-a-new-legend-begins?p=539524#post539524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mundane is probably going to be the same for Origins. Daredevil will probably be the same for Hero. So the TN will be 8 for that. I think that they may use 7 for the TN for Demi-god and, lastly, 6 for the full fledged dieties. This makes it where Apollo would have an easier time of getting 6 successes with a pool of 10 dice than, say, Jeb the Janitor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am also expecting that the scale mechanics make it so that exactly what Apollo can accomplish with 6 successes (at least on tasks in which he is divinely competent) is a lot more than what Jeb can do with those 6 successes, instead of making it so Apollo accomplishes divine feats by having dozens of successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T15:50:31-07:00","id":540093,"title":"","content":"Oh, <i>heck</i> yeah! An excerpt from the <b>Mage Chronicler's Guide</b> for those of you who don't have it:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Scaling is a system designed to allow truly stupendous supernatural feats. It hinges on a simple idea: the way things look and feel in the story can be separated from their dramatic impact \u2014 in other words, blowing up a building doesn't mean you need to throw a double handful of dice at players for damage.<br /> <br /> Scaling can be added to any system. The game nota-tion is a Scaling Rank, attached to an existing game trait such as a rote, Attribute, or Skill. <br /> <br /> \u2022 SFX is short for \u201cSpecial Effects.\u201d This Scaling element describes the multiplier you should apply to successes, or to the trait itself for resisted rolls in situations involving minor characters and story elements, such as scenery, bystanders, and minor combatants (\u201cmooks,\u201d or Extras as defined in Ac-tion Horror on p. 20). You can play fast and loose with these \u201cvirtual successes\u201d so that (for example) a character who scores 200 SFX successes knocks down a dozen helicopters instead of having to get them one at a time. <br /> <br /> \u2022 Impact is how much the Scaled trait actually affects characters and other elements that are central to the story. Add it to each trait in an applicable dice pool, to the resistance penalty it confers (this includes Defense subtracting from dice pools), and to equipment, each based on their respective Scale ratings. The bonus stacks with each trait, so that Elite Strength (+1) and Incredible Brawl (+4) adds a total of five dice to the combined pool</span> </div> </div> </div>Bear in mind that I don't expect the mechanics of the Tiers in Sardonyx to even <i>remotely</i> resemble the above; but I <i>do</i> think it illustrates the sorts of principles that will be in play. For instance, I'm taking the bit about adjusting the target number based on your Tier as being Sardonyx' implementation of the Impact concept described above; and it won't surprise me one bit if the Effects that you can buy with your successes are often Tier-dependent, with that being the way that Sardonyx implements the SFX concept described above. So if you're operating on a Godlike Tier, you'll be rolling against a lower target number (people have been assuming that it bottoms out at 6; but I could see it going as low as 3 or 4) and thus getting more successes; and the Effects that you can buy with a success will be more along the lines of \u201clift a mountain\u201d rather than \u201clift a man\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T17:05:06-07:00","id":540176,"title":"","content":"The only think i'd like to see different is that Impact is automatic rather than rolled. I really don't want to be rolling 16x10^14 dice. That gets frustrating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T17:18:22-07:00","id":540180,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't be shocked to see Demigod or God levels have double-9s or Double-8s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T17:44:19-07:00","id":540211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/537804-the-heart-of-the-sardonyx-system-is-revealed-a-new-legend-begins?p=540176#post540176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only think i'd like to see different is that Impact is automatic rather than rolled. I really don't want to be rolling 16x10^14 dice. That gets frustrating.</div> </div> </div> </div>That appears to be a non-issue; the article is very clear that nearly all dice pools will top out at ten dice, with the most notable exception being those cases where Focus lets you convert Momentum into more dice. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PHGraves</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/537804-the-heart-of-the-sardonyx-system-is-revealed-a-new-legend-begins?p=540180#post540180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't be shocked to see Demigod or God levels have double-9s or Double-8s.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or even double-7s or Double-6s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T19:05:44-07:00","id":540352,"title":"","content":"I figured as much, just speaking muh mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T21:36:52-07:00","id":540576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/537804-the-heart-of-the-sardonyx-system-is-revealed-a-new-legend-begins?p=539130#post539130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really liking the lowered threshold for what needs a roll, complex but not overtly difficult actions and narratively awesome and unique actions can just be hand-waved to succeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have been thinking more on this and though it is hard to make a judgement just from the draft I want to revise my opinion. In the first example with the surgeon doing a complex but everyday operation in a optimal setting I totally agree on hand-waving any rolls, in the same way that I feel like many world building/downtime rolls can be handwaved. But in the second example where the player drops a grenade in the baddies pocket, personally I feel that is an action that should take a roll. If the system is going to have options for Consolations upon failures I think it is more compelling to always have the potential for failure. If the Player failed to get the grenade in the baddies pocket you could always have a Consolation of the baddie diving to the ground away from the grenade now rolling at his feet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T06:08:03-07:00","id":541066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/537804-the-heart-of-the-sardonyx-system-is-revealed-a-new-legend-begins?p=540576#post540576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But in the second example where the player drops a grenade in the baddies pocket, personally I feel that is an action that should take a roll. If the system is going to have options for Consolations upon failures I think it is more compelling to always have the potential for failure. If the Player failed to get the grenade in the baddies pocket you could always have a Consolation of the baddie diving to the ground away from the grenade now rolling at his feet.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's certainly between you and the Director, though for me, it really depends in whether the baddie is a mook or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T07:36:35-07:00","id":541171,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I was torn with that particular description, because I've had those games, someone describes something awesome and <i>just barely</i>...misses. And its awful and I wish I could just wave it away <b>but</b> then, what are dice for... BUT if we're talking a mook giant, well then. That actually does change everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T09:01:33-07:00","id":541338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/537804-the-heart-of-the-sardonyx-system-is-revealed-a-new-legend-begins?p=541171#post541171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I was torn with that particular description, because I've had those 