path.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/537804-the-heart-of-the-sardonyx-system-is-revealed-a-new-legend-begins?p=547488#post547488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keeping it lean, they said, want us hungry for Tuesday they said...</div> </div> </div> </div>Then one of the Children started rampaging. Who's going to clean up the mess?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T16:27:59-07:00","id":547677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/537804-the-heart-of-the-sardonyx-system-is-revealed-a-new-legend-begins?p=547488#post547488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keeping it lean, they said, want us hungry for Tuesday they said...</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, I was promised more by Tuesday, and it's already half twelve on Wednesday. What makes these designers think they can play around with the clock?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T16:34:15-07:00","id":547684,"title":"","content":"Damned dealers is what they are, but instead of pushin' smack and tar their pushin' dreams. and only the first taste is free... they gotta make us crave it or else we won't come back for more. We won't be willing to spend our last penny. I'll show 'em though, I already got my kids listed on Craig's list so I can put up ALL THE MONEY when the Kickstarter comes around. <br /> <br /> Anyone else itchy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T21:11:20-07:00","id":547968,"title":"","content":"New post is up. <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/codename-sardonyx-teaser-the-second/\" target=\"_blank\">Teaser the Second</a>: Attributes and Skills","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T22:31:27-07:00","id":548018,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/537804-the-heart-of-the-sardonyx-system-is-revealed-a-new-legend-begins?p=547968#post547968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New post is up. <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/codename-sardonyx-teaser-the-second/\" target=\"_blank\">Teaser the Second</a>: Attributes and Skills</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh wow this looks interesting, I'm liking the idea that abilities in some instances can be stand ins for merits like contacts. Also this note is interesting...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was very important to the team to allow you to create characters who didn\u2019t exist in a vacuum, but lived, breathed, and interacted with the setting even before you created them*<br /> <br /> * except for <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enkidu\" target=\"_blank\">a certain type of Scion</a>\u2026but that\u2019s another blog post.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes me think we might see some &quot;shaped&quot; scions, heroes created full cloth by the gods rather than being conceived in the more traditional sense. Enkidu fits the bill for someone created rather than born, so would Wonderwoman shaped from clay, or even Athena birthed from Zeus's skull.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T22:51:23-07:00","id":548029,"title":"","content":"Yeah I got a character in a Aztec-centric chronicle who would fit the &quot;whole cloth&quot; concept to a T. <br /> <br /> I myself LOVE that Attributes are categorized by function rather than arena... though I could also see it the other way... maybe its a player choice? Also, with the &quot;skill trick&quot; angle I'm guessing that beginning skill dots are maybe a bit fewer?<br /> <br /> Hmm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T07:11:48-07:00","id":548469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/537804-the-heart-of-the-sardonyx-system-is-revealed-a-new-legend-begins?p=548018#post548018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This makes me think we might see some &quot;shaped&quot; scions, heroes created full cloth by the gods rather than being conceived in the more traditional sense. Enkidu fits the bill for someone created rather than born, so would Wonderwoman shaped from clay, or even Athena birthed from Zeus's skull.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there are multiple ways to make a Scion, and the resulting Scions are slightly different from one another as a result. <i>One</i> way doesn't even require divine parentage, precisely (though you do need to be a child of portent or royalty, possibly with a latent divine heritage).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 06-10-2015, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T08:03:56-07:00","id":548561,"title":"","content":"I LOVE Latent heritage characters! I always just allowed them to be regular scions in 1st ed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T09:06:55-07:00","id":548770,"title":"","content":"I'm wary of the autosucceed Skill Tricks. Things related to combat, movement or environment sure, those can work with autosucceed, but always seeing through lies or traps etc. then not having a Skill Trick that does the reverse of always beating attempts to see through lies or traps can unbalance attempts to present antagonists who are master liars or deceivers or doom trap fortresses.<br /> <br /> Now maybe this is covered in rules related to Contested actions I've missed, if so, disregard, but if Contested actions just involve setting Difficulties, autosucceed Skill Tricks or mechanics should be very careful in how they play out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T09:48:49-07:00","id":548830,"title":"","content":"I think the Skill Tricks sound awesome. I've been houseruling such things with my friends for quite a while, anyway, so this is a great thing for me and mine.<br /> <br /> Everything I hear about this new system is sounding great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:08:35-07:00","id":548882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/537804-the-heart-of-the-sardonyx-system-is-revealed-a-new-legend-begins?p=548469#post548469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, there are multiple ways to make a Scion, and the resulting Scions are slightly different from one another as a result. <i>One</i> way doesn't even require divine parentage, precisely (though you do need to be a child of portent or royalty, possibly with a latent divine heritage).</div> </div> </div> </div>Now you have me thinking of King Arthur or Siddhartha Gautama, people who were born to do great things not because they are the child of a divine being, simply because fate dictated it need be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:12:38-07:00","id":548931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/537804-the-heart-of-the-sardonyx-system-is-revealed-a-new-legend-begins?p=548882#post548882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now you have me thinking of King Arthur or Siddhartha Gautama, people who were born to do great things not because they are the child of a divine being, simply because fate dictated it need be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are both very fertile lines of thought for Scion 2e, although they may not be Scions proper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T13:28:00-07:00","id":549236,"title":"","content":"While in general I really like what I'm seeing, my experience with certain Exalted Charms makes me weary of the auto-succeed Skill Tricks. I mean, I can't know all the system interactions of that yet, but it is a yellow flag for me. On the other hand, it &quot;just&quot; means you automatically overcome the difficulty, right? It might not give you much to work with in terms of Effect and taking care of Complications. Like, you can guarantee a hit with Martial Artist, but if you need a phenomenal hit for some reason, you'll need to roll?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T14:40:56-07:00","id":549392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/537804-the-heart-of-the-sardonyx-system-is-revealed-a-new-legend-begins?p=549236#post549236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While in general I really like what I'm seeing, my experience with certain Exalted Charms makes me weary of the auto-succeed Skill Tricks. I mean, I can't know all the system interactions of that yet, but it is a yellow flag for me. On the other hand, it &quot;just&quot; means you automatically overcome the difficulty, right? It might not give you much to work with in terms of Effect and taking care of Complications. Like, you can guarantee a hit with Martial Artist, but if you need a phenomenal hit for some reason, you'll need to roll?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In my opinion -- Neall can feel free to clarify otherwise -- I'd make the player roll. Regardless of the outcome of the roll, the attack hits (so Failure Is Not An Option). However, extra successes could be used to buy off Complications or to generate additional Effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T20:58:27-07:00","id":549727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/537804-the-heart-of-the-sardonyx-system-is-revealed-a-new-legend-begins?p=549392#post549392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In my opinion -- Neall can feel free to clarify otherwise -- I'd make the player roll. Regardless of the outcome of the roll, the attack hits (so Failure Is Not An Option). However, extra successes could be used to buy off Complications or to generate additional Effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope that is not the case, haha. Barring something in the system existing that somehow makes it not a problem, that would make it the sort of thing I'm worried about, the &quot;press button to bypass story issue&quot; problem Exalted has. In combat it might not be so bad, but in many intellectual and social endeavors it might be troublesome.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Skill Tricks, I have a question: Practical and Potential maximum Attributes exist in the system &quot;mostly for managing dice pools&quot;. But isn't that idea kinda going at cross purposes with all these Skill Tricks that can add an entire additional Skill to a pool?<br /> <br /> The Potential is never more than one dot higher than the Practical maximum in the table shown, though needing to be god to reach <i>seven</i> certainly helps with with over-inflation of the pool. But is that really gonna be enough when you can put an additional 5 (or more) dice in there with a Skill Trick?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T08:48:10-07:00","id":550182,"title":"","content":"I would rule it that you could either use the autosucceed trick or roll and hope for extras, but not both.<br /> I don't have too much issue with autosucceed tricks to advance plot\\story, but I do play a lot of Gumshoe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T14:39:23-07:00","id":550722,"title":"","content":"Honestly I think would only let the auto-succeed rule be applied to trivial tasks, and there aren't many situations in combat that I would consider trivial, fighting a swarm of rats, a mob of citizens possessed by the wrath of Ares, or an entire graveyard of raised skeletons maybe? One of the biggest things that made me cringe playing 2e exalted were those situations where the numbers/game dictated that there was no chance of failure or no chance of success even during the most cinematic of moments. Does the militant Scion need to roll to hit one of hundreds of slow skeletons...probably not, does that same scion need to roll to hit one of a half dozen wights guarding the tomb of a long dead god...definitely!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T17:00:28-07:00","id":550872,"title":"","content":"I'm not talking about the general rules for automatically letting players succeed at things. I am specifically talking about the Skill Tricks of the &quot;spend a point from the Black Pool to automatically X&quot; variety. If you limit them to trivial tasks, you might as well remove them from the game, because nobody is gonna buy a Skill Trick <i>and </i>spend from the black pool for a trivial task.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I'm afraid they might be too powerful as they are now. Why engage with the whole gambler's fallacy thing and accumulate a bunch of points in the black pool to try a massive roll, if I can just spend one point and automatically succeed?<br /> <br /> As for the Exalted comparison, just look at <i>Lie Detector</i>, which looks like it could be a problem for intrigue and mystery stories almost as readily as Exalted's <i>Judge's Ears Technique</i>. It is the same issue of investing character resources making a character great at something - thus indicating to the Director that you want your character to face that kind of challenge - and in so doing acquiring powers that just solve that challenge by themselves, without the player actually engaging with that problem in any really meaningful manner. It is one of the things the EX3 Devs explicitly set out to correct, and I hope Sardonyx* won't fall in that trap.<br /> <br /> Now, if you could get more information out of determining lies (why are they lying? Which part of that statement was a lie?) by rolling, or got a chance to do a superior attack (at the risk of missing) by not using Martial Artist, that might be enough to balance it somewhat, or maybe there is some other nuance of the system that I have not noticed or is not present in the previews so far that prevents the &quot;press button to skip plot&quot; issue of auto-success Tricks, but it still makes me weary for now.<br /> <br /> *<span style=\"font-size:9px\">By the way, the spell-checker here thinks that is not a word. Someone feed it a geology or gem-cutting book or something ^_^</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T19:28:58-07:00","id":550997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/537804-the-heart-of-the-sardonyx-system-is-revealed-a-new-legend-begins?p=550872#post550872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not talking about the general rules for automatically letting players succeed at things. I am specifically talking about the Skill Tricks of the &quot;spend a point from the Black Pool to automatically X&quot; variety. If you limit them to trivial tasks, you might as well remove them from the game, because nobody is gonna buy a Skill Trick<i>and </i>spend from the black pool for a trivial task.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I'm afraid they might be too powerful as they are now. Why engage with the whole gambler's fallacy thing and accumulate a bunch of points in the black pool to try a massive roll, if I can just spend one point and automatically succeed?<br /> <br /> As for the Exalted comparison, just look at <i>Lie Detector</i>, which looks like it could be a problem for intrigue and mystery stories almost as readily as Exalted's <i>Judge's Ears Technique</i>. It is the same issue of investing character resources making a character great at something - thus indicating to the Director that you want your character to face that kind of challenge - and in so doing acquiring powers that just solve that challenge by themselves, without the player actually engaging with that problem in any really meaningful manner. It is one of the things the EX3 Devs explicitly set out to correct, and I hope Sardonyx* won't fall in that trap.<br /> <br /> Now, if you could get more information out of determining lies (why are they lying? Which part of that statement was a lie?) by rolling, or got a chance to do a superior attack (at the risk of missing) by not using Martial Artist, that might be enough to balance it somewhat, or maybe there is some other nuance of the system that I have not noticed or is not present in the previews so far that prevents the &quot;press button to skip plot&quot; issue of auto-success Tricks, but it still makes me weary for now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oops poor reading comprehension, I didn't realize you were talking specifically about skill tricks. I think with the skill tricks there needs to be a way to temper their effectiveness in certain situations, in narratively powerful moments or against narratively powerful enemies I would rather see them just be a bonus rather than an automatic success. You have gathered these points through failures and setbacks, I don't feel like they should be spent to create <b>automatic</b> victories but rather to give you a <b>solid chance</b> to turn things around. When the hero of the story gets knocked down they don't just jump back up and deliver a definitive counter attack, they have to strive to take back control of the fight. I see the black dice representing this drive or struggle to overcome.<br /> <br /> Haha Judges Ear is such a bane on good narratives especially because it is such an early charm, being able to perfectly pick up every lie is such hindrance to the storyteller. It really should have been a higher essence charm with a couple less absolutely powerful but more informative charms below it. Eye of the Unconquered Sun had some of the same problems invalidating major elements of other splats like Lunar shape shifting and Sidereal resplendent destinies, but at least it was essence 5.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T20:52:59-07:00","id":551037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/537804-the-heart-of-the-sardonyx-system-is-revealed-a-new-legend-begins?p=550997#post550997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haha Judges Ear is such a bane on good narratives especially because it is such an early charm, being able to perfectly pick up every lie is such hindrance to the storyteller.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but what I think really makes JET considerably more troublesome than Lie Detector is that the Solar Charm last a whole damn scene! And for a cost that could end up as a net-positive if the player is good at stunting! At least with Lie Detector the character would be quickly extinguishing the black pool if unveiling a lot of lies in a short time. It could still wreck a lot of plots, though<br /> <br /> And yeah, turning auto-success into some sort of bonus depending on circumstances might be a way to make it work without bypassing engagement with the narrative. I mean, sure, if you are the future god of detectives, normal people will certainly have a hard time lying to you, but a powerful trickster spirit or the future god of intrigue might achieve it.<br /> <br /> But anyway, I just wanted to raise a flag to a potential issue. I don't wanna seem like I'm nerd-raging over an incomplete system preview ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T22:50:48-07:00","id":551142,"title":"","content":"So... Do we think the sheet'll have two slots under each skill for the tricks that pop up whenever they get 2 or 4 dots?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T05:35:09-07:00","id":551279,"title":"","content":"Not sold one way or the other on skill tricks, I'd prefer them to let you do something new with a skill rather than an automatic success.<br /> <br /> I'm currently worried that the black pool is going to be the only resource players have. Legend Points had the problem with the weird scaling* (although they could still be burned through quickly with high level powers), butI found them flavourful and useful. I hope that this is just that they are revealing the base system, and the Scion previews will reveal that Legend Points are still used to fuel Boons and Knacks.<br /> <br /> Upset at the lack of Epic Attributes, because I thought they just needed a bit of refinement to work really well, but if Knacks allow me to simulate Epic Attributes (e.g. Epic Strength: your Target Number on Might rolls is one lower than normal**, or enhancing the power of extras I buy) then I can live without them.<br /> <br /> *I have no problem with the mechanism used, except that it means that characters begin with little enough legend that they are relying on stunting, and end up with the most powerful abilities (*cough* untouchable opponent and god-level epic Dex*** *cough*) requiring an expenditure that is negligible<br /> ** I expect that this example is horribly unbalanced for one reason or another, but I'll leave actually designing the system to the Designers.<br /> *** At Hero level I actually think that this knack is alright, with it requiring expenditure of a limited resource for a bonus that can be overcome by raw skill. It's only Demigod and God that I see the problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":4507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","user":"TwoDSix","date":". 06-12-2015, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T09:46:08-07:00","id":551731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/537804-the-heart-of-the-sardonyx-system-is-revealed-a-new-legend-begins?p=550872#post550872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why engage with the whole gambler's fallacy thing and accumulate a bunch of points in the black pool to try a massive roll, if I can just spend one point and automatically succeed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because rolling a lot of dice means you can buy off more Complications and add more Effects to your roll. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T09:55:45-07:00","id":551742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/537804-the-heart-of-the-sardonyx-system-is-revealed-a-new-legend-begins?p=551279#post551279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm currently worried that the black pool is going to be the only resource players have.</div> </div> </div> </div>It won't be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T10:27:30-07:00","id":551816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/537804-the-heart-of-the-sardonyx-system-is-revealed-a-new-legend-begins?p=551731#post551731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because rolling a lot of dice means you can buy off more Complications and add more Effects to your roll.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. It depends on what &quot;automatically succeed&quot; turns out to be. For instance, if it gives you enough successes to clear the difficulty, then you get to roll your dice pool for extra successes, that could end up with more than when rolling a bunch of extra dice, especially at high difficulties. Not to mention things like Lie Detector, which makes you auto-succeed <b>and </b>clears one Complication.<br /> <br /> I mean, OK, unless it turns out to be horribly designed, there will be times when spending the entire black pool and hope you get a fuckton of successes would be the choice over automatically succeeding. I was just exaggerating for effect (much like when I said nobody would buy a Skill Trick and spend from the black pool on a trivial task. It is likely that <i>someone </i>out there would actually do so). But depending on how auto-success works, that use of the pool will become a lot more of an edge case, turning the dynamic swings it would otherwise introduce into something that happens relatively rarely.<br /> <br /> That is a minor concern, though, as I don't think it will turn out that badly designed. I'm more worried about the auto-succeed Tricks resolving the plot instead of the characters doing so, which was one of the problems that complicated my Exalted games. I mean, there is nothing there like &quot;I want my Eclipse to be a terrorist / revolutionary! I will take all these social Charms here. Ok, I wanna start by influencing the local artistic circle, fostering among them resentment towards the ruling family. After that I will join that guild so I can subvert it to my own ends and...&quot; &quot;NO, no. Look at your Charms, you just need to give a single pamphlet to any random peasant and BOOM! Revolution!&quot; but I'm still seeing the potential for trouble, especially in the Procedural and Intrigue areas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png